# Renault 17 two-door coupe, 1972-1979.
#
# The Renault 17, the fastback coupe of the 15/17 pair, on sale from 1972 and
# built until August 1979. UK sales ran through the same period.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renault_17 (cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.255 x 1.640 x 1.310 m, wheelbase 2.440 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes, from the Renault 15/17 dimension box. The hull measures 4.255 m
# on a 2.440 m wheelbase (57.3 per cent) and 1.640 m wide.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation of a yellow 1976 car,
# used directly; image 2 supplied the twin round headlamps in their wide
# recess, the slim centre grille and the bumper with overriders; image 3 the
# fastback hatch, the louvred rear quarter window and the wide tail lamps.
#
# Colours: no British-market names were established, so the objects carry plain
# names: red, blue, white and silver. Weights red 3, blue 3, white 2, silver 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 165 km/h, the 17 TS's quoted maximum. Comfort 55/265, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 55: a low, firm-riding coupe of its era. Classes 2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1972 intro, retires staggered 1989-1992 on a
# seventeen- to twenty-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-17.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-17.dae (146 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-17/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the cabin is slightly taller than the photograph and the
# rubbing strip is interrupted in places. At 128 px the low fastback, the
# louvred quarter window and the twin round lamps read as the Renault 17.

obj=citycar
name=Renault17(Red)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1972
intro_month=1
retire_year=1992
retire_month=6
speed=165
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=55
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=265

Image[E]=./images/renault-17-red_E.0.0,-33,14
